         "True",
         "True",
         "False",
         "True",
         "Prohibits algorithms used to determine access to important opportunities (e.g., employment) or information about them in Washington D.C. from discriminating on the basis of protected classes; also mandates related algorithm audits, disclosures, and remedies for decisions made based on inaccurate data.",
         "Prohibits entities in Washington D.C. from determining eligibility for, or access to information about, \"important life opportunities\" (e.g., housing or employment) on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, familial status, source of income, or disability in a discriminatory manner.\n\nRequires entities to provide a public notice describing any algorithmic tools they use to determine eligibility for, or access to information about, important life opportunities. The notice must be sent to any individual about whom such a determination is made.\n\nRequires the notice described above to cover the data collected by algorithmic tools and how that data is shared externally, how that data informs the tool's decisions, and the rights provided under this act.\n\nRequires entities to provide notice, to any individual against whom they take any adverse action (e.g., firing) on the basis of an algorithmic determination, that the individual may access and submit corrections to any personal information considered by the algorithm. A human must then redo the decision based on the corrected information.  \n\nRequires entities to audit their algorithmic decision-making tools before deployment and annually thereafter to analyze discriminatory effects and other impacts, and then implement reasonable measures to address findings of unlawful disparate impact. Entities must submit a report on the audit to the DC government.\n\nPermits affected individuals or the DC Attorney General to file a civil action in response to violations of this law, with fines up to $10,000 per violation.",
